Z||000000||Alex2004||05-05-2001||02:17 PM||||We just bought a new fan relay for an 84 SE from GM but the fan still doesn't come on w/ A/c on.  I know the fan works because i have 'hotwired' from the hot wire to the 2nd big BLACK wire on the plug in, but when i do it to the first one nothing happenes. i'm guess those are for the different speeds?  Do any of you know what's wrong?  Do you think i might needa replace the ceramic thing near the fan motor?  Please let me know!  Thanks<P>Alex...<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Alex2004||05-05-2001||07:11 PM||||~*BUMP*~||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||05-05-2001||10:29 PM||||You have a 2 speed fan.<P>There are 2 relays. One for each speed. <P>High speed only comes on if the engine hits 241F.<P>Low works with A/C on or above 221F<P>Main power to the relay is red.<P>The wires to the fan...<P>The black/pink wire is high.<BR>The black/red is low.<P>The all black at the fan connector is ground.<P>If you can get the fan to run on the black/pink then the motor is good.<P>If the black/red won't kick it over then the resistor on the fan frame is bad.<P>There are more notes in my cave.||||reg||1
